# THE OPEN SIGNAL — a feature-length film for KSAB-TV, channel 7, the 18:00 Saturday block.
#
# In-universe: a 2.5-hour period picture about the eight years after The Handoff when
# the transmitters stayed up and nobody owned them, and what went out on them — for
# free, all night, to a Basin with nothing else on — was pornography. It is about a
# nineteen-year-old dishwasher who was dealt exactly one card, the director who
# believed a filthy picture could still hold an audience for ninety minutes, the family
# they built in a rented house, and the licensing authority that came back and made
# every one of them a criminal in an afternoon.
#
# ADULT. The subject is the adult-broadcast trade and the film says so plainly — the
# work, the money, the shoots, and what the trade costs the people in it. It depicts;
# it does not perform. Scheduled at 21:00 for that reason.
#
# The film is a RECORDING. Its cast are display names in ::cast, never npc_ ids —
# nothing here spawns a studio NPC and nothing presence-gates. See docs/bsm-format.md.

::cast
DEACON | Deacon Vox | the one card
DENNY | Denny Faust | the dishwasher, before
AUGGIE | Auggie Prine | the director
SABLE | Marguerite Sable | the leading lady, and the mother of the house
KESTREL | Kestrel | never takes the headset off
REED | Reed Halloran | the best friend
BUCK | Buck Ozarow | wants an honest shop
WILBY | Wilby Crane | the sound man
VAL | Val Crane | his wife
SCOTTY | Scotty Kell | the boom
COLONEL | The Colonel | the money
TODD | Todd Vane | the problem
GONDOLLI | Fisk Gondolli | the man from the Coast
RASHAD | Rashad Ghazi | the house on the hill
MAURICE | Maurice Tam | the roadhouse, and the man who tried
JOANIE | Joanie Faust | mother
CLERK | the licensing clerk | Reclamation Authority
BOY | the boy with the flares |
::endcast

