KESTREL:
I’d be somewhere with a set on, listening to somebody else be you.

She says it flatly, without self-pity, the way seventeen-year-olds say the truest thing they will ever say and then never mention it again.

DEACON:
Kestrel.

KESTREL:
Don’t.

DEACON:
