GONDOLLI:
No. But it’s a business, and the difference between us, Auggie, is that I have never once needed it to be a picture.

Auggie Prine looks at the ugly little rig on the table for a long time.

AUGGIE:
Get it off my table.

GONDOLLI:
Sure.

He closes the case. He is still smiling. He was always going to be smiling, because he was never asking.

GONDOLLI:
I’ll leave the number, Auggie. Everybody calls the number eventually. The Colonel already did.

AUGGIE:
The Colonel did what?

GONDOLLI:
Ah. He hasn’t told you.

